# Branch, PR & release guardrails

PostForge is a **template app repo** — not an npm package. Follow branch-first development and manual GitHub Releases.

## Read first

- [docs/contributing.md](../docs/contributing.md) — branches, PRs, commits, pre-PR checklist
- [docs/releasing.md](../docs/releasing.md) — manual releases, version invariant, recovery
- [docs/CURRENT_PRODUCT_SURFACE.md](../docs/CURRENT_PRODUCT_SURFACE.md) — update when routes/endpoints change
- [CHANGELOG.md](../CHANGELOG.md) — `## [Unreleased]` for in-progress changes

## Branches

- Base: **`main`** only (no `develop`).
- Create `feature/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, or `chore/` branches before substantive work.
- **Never** commit or push to `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Never** merge PRs, approve PRs, or run destructive git commands unless explicitly asked.

## Commits & PRs

- Use Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, …).
- Commit **only when asked** — otherwise leave work uncommitted or on a feature branch.
- Open PRs with `gh pr create` **only when asked**.
- Before declaring code work complete: run **`npm run validate`**, update tests, `CHANGELOG.md`, and `CURRENT_PRODUCT_SURFACE.md` when applicable.

## Releases (agents)

- Version source: **`VERSION`** ⟺ tag **`vX.Y.Z`** ⟺ GitHub Release **`vX.Y.Z`**.
- **Do not** run `.github/workflows/release.yml`, create tags, or create GitHub Releases without explicit user approval.
- **Do not** commit release metadata to `main` — only the release workflow may do that.

## Auth package

- Consume `@tgoliveira/secure-auth` via public exports only — do not modify the package or its schema from PostForge unless explicitly requested.
